### PDB

The Protein Data Bank (PDB) is the primary database for experimentally determined three-dimensional structures of proteins, nucleic acids,
and other biological macromolecules. It provides structural files in formats such as PDB and mmCIF, along with detailed information about
molecular architecture and experimental methods. In this project, PDB was used to obtain protein structure files for visualization,
refinement, and structural validation using different bioinformatics tools.

